WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.013
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.313 --> 00:00:08.375
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:15.158
Unit eighteen: Science and Innovation. In this unit, you will talk about inventions, science and future plans.

4
00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:17.047
researcher.

5
00:00:17.747 --> 00:00:22.184
researcher means a person who studies something carefully to discover new facts.

6
00:00:22.484 --> 00:00:25.076
The researcher is testing a new rice variety.

7
00:00:25.776 --> 00:00:27.975
Your turn. Say: researcher.

8
00:00:30.675 --> 00:00:31.665
researcher.

9
00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:33.790
3D printing.

10
00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:39.137
3D printing means making solid objects from a digital design, layer by layer.

11
00:00:39.437 --> 00:00:42.331
Doctors are using 3D printing to make body parts.

12
00:00:43.031 --> 00:00:45.486
Your turn. Say: 3D printing.

13
00:00:48.186 --> 00:00:49.605
3D printing.

14
00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:51.885
electric vehicle.

15
00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:56.523
electric vehicle means a car or bike that runs on electricity.

16
00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:59.589
More electric vehicles are appearing in Phnom Penh.

17
00:01:00.289 --> 00:01:02.918
Your turn. Say: electric vehicle.

18
00:01:05.618 --> 00:01:06.909
electric vehicle.

19
00:01:07.917 --> 00:01:08.639
gene.

20
00:01:09.339 --> 00:01:12.802
gene means a part of a cell that controls features like eye colour.

21
00:01:13.102 --> 00:01:15.635
Scientists have found a gene linked to the disease.

22
00:01:16.335 --> 00:01:18.395
Your turn. Say: gene.

23
00:01:21.095 --> 00:01:21.922
gene.

24
00:01:22.917 --> 00:01:24.185
vaccine development.

25
00:01:24.885 --> 00:01:28.428
vaccine development means the process of creating a new vaccine.

26
00:01:28.728 --> 00:01:31.343
Vaccine development usually takes many years.

27
00:01:32.043 --> 00:01:35.172
Your turn. Say: vaccine development.

28
00:01:37.872 --> 00:01:39.256
vaccine development.

29
00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:41.599
invention patent.

30
00:01:42.299 --> 00:01:46.215
invention patent means a legal document that protects a new invention.

31
00:01:46.515 --> 00:01:48.990
She got an invention patent for her water filter.

32
00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:52.435
Your turn. Say: invention patent.

33
00:01:55.135 --> 00:01:56.612
invention patent.

34
00:01:57.617 --> 00:01:58.653
robotics.

35
00:01:59.353 --> 00:02:02.699
robotics means the science of designing and building robots.

36
00:02:02.999 --> 00:02:05.115
Our school has a new robotics club.

37
00:02:05.815 --> 00:02:07.863
Your turn. Say: robotics.

38
00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:11.762
robotics.

39
00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:13.391
drone.

40
00:02:14.091 --> 00:02:17.588
drone means a small aircraft without a pilot, controlled from the ground.

41
00:02:17.888 --> 00:02:20.236
Farmers use drones to check their fields.

42
00:02:20.936 --> 00:02:22.788
Your turn. Say: drone.

43
00:02:25.488 --> 00:02:26.384
drone.

44
00:02:27.383 --> 00:02:29.394
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:29.694 --> 00:02:32.077
What are you doing this weekend, Mr. Daniel?

46
00:02:33.383 --> 00:02:35.801
I'm visiting a robotics exhibition on Saturday.

47
00:02:37.117 --> 00:02:41.151
Sounds great! I'm going to learn about 3D printing next month.

48
00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:46.147
Excellent. Do you think electric vehicles will replace motorbikes?

49
00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:49.856
I think they will, but it will take time.

50
00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:54.624
The exhibition starts at nine, so I'll pick you up at eight thirty.

51
00:02:55.917 --> 00:02:58.218
Grammar focus: Future forms.

52
00:02:58.518 --> 00:03:00.959
Use will for predictions and quick decisions.

53
00:03:01.259 --> 00:03:05.418
Use going to for plans, and the present continuous for fixed arrangements.

54
00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:10.167
For example: I'm going to study engineering, and we're meeting the researcher at ten.

55
00:03:10.467 --> 00:03:13.988
Use the present simple for timetables: The exhibition starts at nine.

56
00:03:14.983 --> 00:03:18.042
Now read and listen. Drones on the Farm.

57
00:03:18.342 --> 00:03:22.547
In Cambodia, a new generation of farmers is starting to use drones.

58
00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:27.696
The drones fly over rice fields and spray fertiliser in a few minutes.

59
00:03:28.983 --> 00:03:31.598
Researchers say this will save water, time and money.

60
00:03:32.883 --> 00:03:36.903
Next year, a local company is going to open a training centre for drone pilots.

61
00:03:38.217 --> 00:03:42.004
Experts predict that smart farming will become normal within ten years.

62
00:03:43.317 --> 00:03:45.969
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:46.269 --> 00:03:48.837
A small aircraft without a pilot is a blank.

64
00:03:49.137 --> 00:03:52.094
A, gene. B, drone. C, robotics.

65
00:03:56.083 --> 00:03:57.723
The answer is B: drone.

66
00:03:59.217 --> 00:04:00.624
I think it blank rain later.

67
00:04:00.924 --> 00:04:03.765
A, will. B, is raining. C, rains.

68
00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:09.494
The answer is A: will.

69
00:04:10.983 --> 00:04:14.495
We blank our grandparents tomorrow. We've already bought the tickets.

70
00:04:14.795 --> 00:04:18.379
A, will visit. B, are visiting. C, visit.

71
00:04:22.383 --> 00:04:24.545
The answer is B: are visiting.

72
00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:28.421
Making objects layer by layer is blank.

73
00:04:28.721 --> 00:04:33.025
A, 3D printing. B, vaccine development. C, invention patent.

74
00:04:37.017 --> 00:04:39.028
The answer is A: 3D printing.

75
00:04:40.517 --> 00:04:43.898
According to the text, what is a local company going to open?

76
00:04:44.198 --> 00:04:50.278
A, a factory. B, a training centre for drone pilots. C, a robotics club.

77
00:04:54.283 --> 00:04:57.595
The answer is B: a training centre for drone pilots.

78
00:04:59.083 --> 00:05:04.023
Now it's your turn to speak. Which invention will change our lives most in the next ten years?

79
00:05:09.323 --> 00:05:13.946
I think electric vehicles will change our cities, because the air will be much cleaner.

80
00:05:14.246 --> 00:05:15.793
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:16.783 --> 00:05:20.724
Great work today! You learned eight new words and future forms.

82
00:05:21.024 --> 00:05:24.652
Today's value is curiosity. Ask questions and find out.

83
00:05:24.952 --> 00:05:27.128
See you in Unit nineteen. Goodbye!

84
00:05:27.428 --> 00:05:30.591
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

